## Upgrade workflow

```bash
npm outdated
npm update                    # minor/patch within semver ranges
# exact pins (next/react/eslint): edit package.json, then npm install
npm run lint && npm run check:urdu && npm run test && npm run build
```

1. Read changelogs for `next`, `sanity`, `next-sanity`, Tailwind, ESLint
2. Never run `npm audit fix --force` if it downgrades Sanity or Next
3. After bump: fix breaking API changes in one focused PR
4. Ship only after `preflight` (+ `build`)

## Pinning exceptions (document here if added)

- **Next / eslint-config-next 16.2.12** — exact matched pair (July 2026 security alignment)
- **React / react-dom 19.2.8** — exact pair with Next
- **ESLint 9.39.4** — exact pin + `overrides.eslint`; ESLint 10 crashes `eslint-config-next` (`getFilename()`). Dependabot ignores ESLint major bumps.
- **TypeScript 6.0.3** — exact pin + `overrides.typescript`; TS 7 breaks `typescript-eslint` (peer `<6.1.0`). Dependabot ignores TypeScript major bumps.
- **`postcss@^8.5.24` override** — patched PostCSS under Next/Tailwind
- **`sharp@^0.35.3` override** — patched libvips CVEs for Next image pipeline
- **`adm-zip@0.6.0` override** — Sanity CLI ZIP advisory
- **`js-yaml@^4.3.0` override** — nested Sanity CLI / Vercel frameworks advisory
- **`smol-toml@^1.7.1` override** — nested Vercel frameworks DoS advisory
- **`typeid-js` → `uuid@^11.1.1`** — nested uuid buffer bounds advisory
- **`minimatch@>=9` → brace-expansion `^5.0.8`** — do not globally override brace-expansion (breaks ESLint minimatch@3)
- **babel-plugin-react-compiler 1.0.0** — required for React Compiler in `next.config.ts`
- No other pins unless an upstream blocker is documented in this file

## Agent behavior

- When touching `package.json`, check `npm outdated` and propose latest compatible versions
- Do not leave stale majors when a safe upgrade path exists
- Update `01-project.mdc` version line only when stack versions change materially
